        "## step 3: Feature Extraction (The NLP Bridge)\n",
        "\n",
        "*Converting raw audio into multi-lingual mathematical representations.*\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **ASR Transcription:** Pass the preprocessed audio through `whisper-small-Sinhala-Fine_Tune`. Store the raw text output.\n",
        "2. **Semantic Embedding:** Pass the text transcripts through the **LaBSE** model to generate **768-dimensional** dense vectors that capture semantic intent in a language-agnostic space.\n",
        "3. **Tensor Conversion:** Convert the NumPy arrays of vectors into PyTorch Tensors.\n",
        "4. \ud83d\udca1 **Crucial Addition - Vector Caching:** Save these final tensors to your Drive using `torch.save(feat, save_path)`. This way, as you tweak your Neural Network in the next phase, you don't have to wait for Whisper to transcribe the audio every single time you run the script.\n",
        "5. \ud83d\udca1 **Crucial Addition - t-SNE Visualization:** Before training the neural network, reduce your 768D vectors to 2D using t-SNE and plot them on a scatter graph. This visually proves that LaBSE successfully grouped Sinhala and English commands into semantic clusters."
      ]
